{"Address_address2":"JINJA North Division","Email":"worldeducarenetwork@gmail.com","Address_address1":"BUTEMBE, BLC Close Kyamagwa, Mafubira Ward","Website1":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/world-educare-network","Website2":"https://www.x.com/WorldEducareNet","Number3":"18","Number2":"15000","Number1":"5000","MultiLine5":"Uganda Police Force for responding to child protection issues; National Environmental Management Authority for information and skilled personnel for advocacy and environmental awareness campaigns; public schools as partners in teacher mentorship and school leadership professional development; government physical infrastructure as free venus for skills development trainings.","SingleLine2":"World Educare Network","MultiLine7":"","SingleLine3":"Immaculate AINEMBABAZI","MultiLine1":"Create Empowered Communities endowed with formal knowledge, skills, values & positive attitude; with individuals sustainably freed from ignorance, poverty & diseases.","SingleLine5":"Chief Executive Officer","MultiLine2":"Amplifying opportunities for inclusive & equitable quality education with accessible resources; prioritizing safe school, good health, livelihood, equality, environment, and sustainability skills.","MultiLine3":"Promoting inclusive & equitable quality education; working with schools, community youth groups & women to advocate for education; directly sponsoring 172 disadvantaged learners (80% are girls, children with disabilities & living with HIV/AIDS).

Health, Livelihood & Gender Equality; engaging local communities against preventable diseases; embracing enterprnuershp & valuable life skills.

Technology, Emplyable Skills, Environment & Climate; working with school children and teachers to improve digital literacy, hands on skills and environmental sustainability.","Address_zipCode":"5241","MultiLine4":"Mentored 6 youths into founders of social enterprises since 2023; more than 250 girls & young women from our skills development trainings are now making and using personal reusable sanitary pads; 3 student led school ICT Clubs we initiated have become innovation and competitive; more than 9 women & youth groups are now making and using soap made by them locally; 4 of our partner schools successfully drafted the child protection policy in 2025 and are implementing them.","Number10":"80","Name_Last":"OKINO","MultipleChoice":["Uganda"],"SingleLine31":"","SingleLine32":"","Dropdown":"Yes","SubForm1":[{"firstName":"Joseph","lastName":"OKINO","email7":"worldeducarenetwork@gmail.com"},{"firstName":"Immaculate","lastName":"AINEMBABAZI","email7":"wenetprojects.ug@gmail.com"}],"MultipleChoice1":["Grade 1","Grade 2","Grade 3","Grade 4","Grade 5","Grade 6","Grade 7","Grade 8","Grade 9","Grade 10","Grade 11","Grade 12"],"MultipleChoice4":null,"MultipleChoice3":["AI and education","Climate and education","Girls education","Inclusive education","Secondary education and work readiness"],"Dropdown9":"Yes","Name5_First":"Joseph","Name5_Last":"OKINO","Dropdown4":"Yes, all of the countries","Dropdown3":"Uganda","Dropdown2":"Non-profit","Dropdown1":"Yes","Dropdown8":"Poor (less than $2 a day)","Dropdown6":"Minimal contribution","SingleLine":"Chief Executive Officer","Dropdown5":"Less than $120","Dropdown10":"Yes","Dropdown11":"Yes","Dropdown13":"Yes, all our schools","Radio2":"Yes","Radio1":"No","Dropdown15":"GSF LinkedIn","MonthYear":"Jun-2020","Website":"wenetuganda.org","Name_First":"Joseph","MultiLine":"","Name4_First":"Joseph","Name4_Last":"OKINO","Number":"18","Email6":"wenetprojects.ug@gmail.com","SubForm":[{"firstName":"Moses","lastName":"Wamanga","jobTitle":"Executive Director","organisation":"KAWA Uganda","email":"kawaagency@gmail.com"},{"firstName":"Titus","lastName":"Mukwano","jobTitle":"Program Manager","organisation":"NeFCoRD","email":"titusmukwano@gmail.com"}],"Email1":"worldeducarenetwork@gmail.com","Email2":"worldeducarenetwork@gmail.com","Address_country":"Uganda","Address_city":"Jinja City"}

